\section{Results}
\label{sec:experiments}

All results are on the common target set of Section~\ref{sec:protocol}, with the factor model (P5) for inference unless a rule is named. The headline subset is the 154 held-out models, from 51 organisations, that can be given 109 benchmarks from the pool (and have at least 37 observed target benchmarks); they are the same at every $k$. The temporal and strength splits have 13 models (4 organisations) and 22 models (11 organisations) in that subset, so their intervals are indicative only (Appendix~\ref{app:data}). Intervals are 90\% group-bootstrap. Selection rules are S0 (random), S1 (most scores among the training models), S2 (largest training standard deviation), S4 (pivoted QR on the completed training matrix~\citep{boutsidis2009css}) and S6 (Section~\ref{sec:method}); the simple inference baselines are P0 (the benchmark mean) and P1 (the mean of the revealed standardised scores).

